# Cloudflare static-assets response headers. They apply to files served from the
# static asset store — the prerendered pages — and NOT to responses the Worker
# renders itself (the EmDash admin at /_emdash/*, its API, anything left
# on-demand). See AGENTS.md "Content Security Policy".
#
# REPORT-ONLY on purpose: violations are logged to the browser console and
# nothing is blocked, so this cannot break a page. Read the console on the
# pages you ship, add what is legitimately needed, then rename the header to
# `Content-Security-Policy` to enforce it.
#
# The two sha256 values are the inline scripts <Head /> emits (the colour-scheme
# bootstrap and the consent-gate stub). They change only when
# @getvitops/astro changes those scripts; regenerate with
#   vp exec node -e "import('@getvitops/astro').then(m => console.log(m.contentSecurityPolicy()))"
# `templates.test.ts` in the toolchain repo guards that they match.
#
# Expect reports for scripts this policy cannot name by hash: EmDash's own head
# tags, a server-island loader, an editor's HTML block, and third-party tags the
# consent gate activates (allow their origins in script-src/connect-src).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-CEiVlTo192T9Rug/nAl+ihvkqOQkYdr6Rq3oc+gR9JU=' 'sha256-z/UqsITVvNGOJSaOSvhN1rdtyYdMIxpQ/lMXM1q0g90='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
